melody:
# Chorus as published in 1927 (cut time, written here with quarter-note beats; 3-beat pickup)
When whip-poor-wills call
G4 Bb4/ C5/ Eb5 C5(4) ~C5
and ev-'ning is nigh,
Eb4 G4/ Bb4/ C5 Bb4(4) ~Bb4
I hur-ry to my blue heav-en.
Bb3 C4/ Eb4/ G4 F4(4) G4(4) F4 Eb4(3) ~Eb4
A turn to the right,
G4 Bb4/ C5/ Eb5 C5(4) ~C5
a lit-tle white light
Eb4 G4/ Bb4/ C5 Bb4(4) ~Bb4
will lead you to my blue heav-en.
Bb3 C4/ Eb4/ G4 F4(4) G4(4) F4 Eb4(3) ~Eb4
You'll see a smil-ing face, a fire-place, a co-zy room,
Eb5 Eb5 Eb5 Eb5 D5 D5 C5 C5 ~Bb4 Bb4 C5 Bb4 Ab4 C5(2) ~C5(3)
a lit-tle nest that's nes-tled where the ros-es bloom.
D5 D5 C5 C5 Bb4 Bb4 Ab4 Ab4 Bb4 Ab4 G4 Bb4(2) ~Bb4
Just Mol-lie and me
G4 Bb4/ C5/ Eb5 C5(4) ~C5
and Ba-by makes three,
Eb4 G4/ Bb4/ C5 Bb4(4) ~Bb4
we're hap-py in my blue heav-en.
Bb3 C4/ Eb4/ G4 F4(4) Bb4(3) ~G4 F4 Eb4(3) r

# Once more
When whip-poor-wills call
G4 Bb4/ C5/ Eb5 C5(4) ~C5
and ev-'ning is nigh,
Eb4 G4/ Bb4/ C5 Bb4(4) ~Bb4
I hur-ry to my blue heav-en.
Bb3 C4/ Eb4/ G4 F4(4) G4(4) F4 Eb4(3) ~Eb4
A turn to the right,
G4 Bb4/ C5/ Eb5 C5(4) ~C5
a lit-tle white light
Eb4 G4/ Bb4/ C5 Bb4(4) ~Bb4
will lead you to my blue heav-en.
Bb3 C4/ Eb4/ G4 F4(4) G4(4) F4 Eb4(3) ~Eb4
You'll see a smil-ing face, a fire-place, a co-zy room,
Eb5 Eb5 Eb5 Eb5 D5 D5 C5 C5 ~Bb4 Bb4 C5 Bb4 Ab4 C5(2) ~C5(3)
a lit-tle nest that's nes-tled where the ros-es bloom.
D5 D5 C5 C5 Bb4 Bb4 Ab4 Ab4 Bb4 Ab4 G4 Bb4(2) ~Bb4
Just Mol-lie and me
G4 Bb4/ C5/ Eb5 C5(4) ~C5
and Ba-by makes three,
Eb4 G4/ Bb4/ C5 Bb4(4) ~Bb4
we're hap-py in my blue heav-en.
Bb3 C4/ Eb4/ G4 F4(4) Bb4(4) C5 Eb5(3) ~Eb5(3) r
